Subject: [PATCH] short-vis-path: canonicalize the manifest source directory

ExpandedPath canonicalizes the call-site source file before removing the
manifest's src directory. On Windows, canonicalization introduces the
verbatim path prefix, while CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR still has an ordinary drive
path. Comparing these representations makes valid module paths fail the
prefix check and causes the attribute macro to panic.

Canonicalize both paths before comparing them. This also resolves symlinked
manifest directories consistently with the call-site source path.

The modified upstream file retains its MPL-2.0 license.

---
 kernel/libs/short-vis-path/src/args.rs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/libs/short-vis-path/src/args.rs b/kernel/libs/short-vis-path/src/args.rs
--- a/kernel/libs/short-vis-path/src/args.rs
+++ b/kernel/libs/short-vis-path/src/args.rs
@@ -162,6 +162,11 @@ impl ExpandedPath {
             let dir = std::env::var("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR").expect("Failed to get manifest dir.");
             std::path::PathBuf::from(dir).join("src")
         };
+        // Both paths must use the same canonical representation, including
+        // Windows verbatim prefixes and any symlinked source directories.
+        let Ok(prefix) = prefix.canonicalize() else {
+            panic!("Unable to canonicalize {prefix:?}.")
+        };
 
         // Strip `$CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR/src/`.
         let Ok(module_path) = local_path.strip_prefix(&prefix) else {
